{"id": "EUVD-2026-103913", "enisaUuid": "31d6b03b-59be-3575-bad9-b69753e089e3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: pressure: rohm-bm1390: Return error when read fails\n\nThe data reading function ignores the cached error value, and\nunconditionally returns 0. Return cached 'ret' -value after stopping\nthe measurement so user knows if read failed and data is garbage.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/493e743ea1b5930bfa0c6c25b46add6c5d5323db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6280d15f08603230855cf667d1cf67e7e94f693c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0e951ffc5a28141a106562997ca136ec6a0e1a3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-36fj-q3xh-9g4g", "CVE-2026-98659"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1309c29e-19fe-3db0-a7bd-4e6fd2a111f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "98e5b68e-6aec-3a46-ac9d-d352f4f8e93a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ae453b2d-45a5-341a-8faf-8f69e227b8d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "caa4dd11-0b53-3775-a786-53fbe17f98e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "534674463a5978c6eda8185b31f5b903a9543f46 <b0e951ffc5a28141a106562997ca136ec6a0e1a3"}, {"id": "cd64ae6e-881a-30d7-bba5-7b4b2237a698", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "da636d49-8de9-3868-add5-531183a9f28d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ef5e87a8-100a-3c06-ad5a-1c390004929f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "534674463a5978c6eda8185b31f5b903a9543f46 <493e743ea1b5930bfa0c6c25b46add6c5d5323db"}, {"